WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.462
<v Therapist>Come on in. What's on your mind this week?

00:00:06.462 --> 00:00:16.846
<v Client>I notice that I make myself small. I do that, it doesn't happen to me. You just get on with it, you don't really think about it.

00:00:17.246 --> 00:00:20.323
<v Therapist>How is it to say it out loud?

00:00:23.323 --> 00:00:28.323
<v Client>It is what it is, there's nothing you can do about it anyway.

00:00:28.723 --> 00:00:30.723
<v Therapist>Mhm, yes.

00:00:31.123 --> 00:00:36.892
<v Client>I realised that I'm afraid of being left. I function, and that's enough for now.

00:00:37.292 --> 00:00:39.292
<v Therapist>Tell me more about that.

00:00:39.692 --> 00:00:44.308
<v Client>Sort of a pressure, in my stomach somehow, but it's nothing much.

00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:46.708
<v Therapist>Mhm.

00:00:47.108 --> 00:00:55.185
<v Client>Sort of a pressure, in my stomach somehow, but it's nothing much. It was okay, nothing terrible, just how it goes.

00:00:55.585 --> 00:01:12.508
<v Client>When my father died I was fifteen, and I didn't cry. I just kept functioning and everyone said how brave I was. I don't think I've cried properly since, and that frightens me, if I'm honest. It's as if there's a door shut somewhere.

00:01:12.908 --> 00:01:17.523
<v Therapist>Let's come back to sleep for a moment. How is that going?

00:01:20.523 --> 00:01:23.215
<v Client>Yeah. Um. Sleep is okay, I think.

00:01:23.615 --> 00:01:32.846
<v Client>Mark said I should take a holiday. As if that would fix anything. I was told to stop making such a fuss about it.

00:01:33.246 --> 00:01:35.246
<v Therapist>Yeah.

00:01:35.646 --> 00:01:42.954
<v Client>You don't want to be a burden to anyone. I should have said something there, but I just didn't.

00:01:43.354 --> 00:01:45.354
<v Therapist>I see.

00:01:45.754 --> 00:01:50.369
<v Client>I felt bad, but don't ask me why, I have no idea.

00:01:50.769 --> 00:01:54.231
<v Therapist>Our nervous system doesn't distinguish between then and now.

00:01:54.631 --> 00:02:02.708
<v Client>Mrs Whitfield from the next office asked how I was and I lied. It's just too much, all at once, constantly.

00:02:03.108 --> 00:02:05.800
<v Therapist>Did you talk to him about it?

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:17.646
<v Client>My mother called, it was the same as ever, exhausting really. It was just a strange week, I guess, hard to say really.

00:02:18.046 --> 00:02:20.046
<v Therapist>Is it often like that?

00:02:23.046 --> 00:02:33.046
<v Client>Mark said I should take a holiday. As if that would fix anything. It is what it is, there's nothing you can do about it anyway.

00:02:33.446 --> 00:02:36.523
<v Therapist>You talk about a rucksack. What's in it?

00:02:39.523 --> 00:02:49.523
<v Client>I felt bad, but don't ask me why, I have no idea. It's like a rucksack I've carried for years, and I only notice it now.

00:02:49.923 --> 00:02:51.923
<v Therapist>Yeah.

00:02:52.323 --> 00:03:00.400
<v Client>I should have said something there, but I just didn't. So I just went home and watched telly the whole evening.

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:03.492
<v Therapist>When did you first have this feeling?

00:03:06.492 --> 00:03:10.723
<v Client>I was told to stop making such a fuss about it.

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:14.969
<v Therapist>What you're describing is called dissociation; it's a protective response.

00:03:15.369 --> 00:03:22.677
<v Client>So I just said nothing, like always. I felt bad, but don't ask me why, I have no idea.

00:03:23.077 --> 00:03:25.077
<v Therapist>I see.

00:03:25.477 --> 00:03:29.708
<v Client>This week was hard, but at least now I know why.

00:03:30.108 --> 00:03:33.185
<v Therapist>You talk about a rucksack. What's in it?

00:03:36.185 --> 00:03:40.415
<v Client>My mother called, it was the same as ever, exhausting really.

00:03:40.815 --> 00:03:43.123
<v Therapist>We have another twenty minutes today.

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:48.138
<v Client>It struck me that I give in immediately whenever my mother calls.

00:03:48.538 --> 00:03:50.538
<v Therapist>I see.

00:03:50.938 --> 00:04:04.015
<v Client>I was ashamed when I said it, quite badly actually. It is what it is, there's nothing you can do about it anyway. My mother called, it was the same as ever, exhausting really.

00:04:04.415 --> 00:04:06.415
<v Therapist>Mhm, yes.

00:04:06.815 --> 00:04:19.123
<v Client>So I just went home and watched telly the whole evening. That's why I'm so tired, I think. Because I'm always on guard. It was okay, nothing terrible, just how it goes.

00:04:19.523 --> 00:04:24.138
<v Therapist>I hear a tiredness in that which is older than this week.

00:04:24.538 --> 00:04:27.231
<v Client>So I just said nothing, like always.

00:04:27.631 --> 00:04:29.631
<v Therapist>That makes complete sense.

00:04:30.031 --> 00:04:43.492
<v Client>I don't know, it was fine, kind of, just a bit off in places. You just keep functioning and somehow it works out. It was just a strange week, I guess, hard to say really.

00:04:43.892 --> 00:04:45.892
<v Therapist>I see.

00:04:46.292 --> 00:04:49.754
<v Therapist>Let's stop there for today. See you next week.

00:04:50.154 --> 00:04:52.846
<v Client>Yes. Thank you. See you next week.
